The Composery automation API, server to menu.

- Server endpoints: /_composery/api/v1/... (API-key auth, in-process on the
  single port) and the unauthenticated /_composery identification probe the
  mobile app uses to validate a URL before embedding it. Mounted before the
  VS Code catch-all so it is not swallowed; gated by the persistence-readiness
  middleware.
- Pty host exposure: the VS Code server hands its IPtyService to the embedder,
  so API-created terminals are ordinary persistent VS Code terminals instead
  of a parallel implementation. They carry API_TERMINAL_WORKSPACE_ID -
  belonging to no window, they belong to whichever window asks: layout merge
  adopts them (except while detaching, so Detach Session is not silently
  undone) and inventory events reach every client, not just the owning
  workspace's. Keep the id in sync with routes/api/terminals.ts; a test pins
  the two together.
- Home-menu entry for managing API keys; the command itself lives in the
  composery-api builtin extension.

